Id: aud009i
Severity: INFO
Category: logging
Check: check_accounting
Fix: Install acct (psacct on Fedora and RHEL) and enable its service.
References: accton(8); acct(5); lastcomm(1); sa(8)
Controls: CIS 8.2, 8.5; NIST AU-2, AU-12; ISO 8.15

No process accounting is installed on this Linux host: no accton
(the acct package on Debian, Ubuntu and Arch, psacct on Fedora and
RHEL). With it on, the kernel appends a record for every process that
exits (command, account, start time, CPU and memory used) to
/var/log/account/pacct or /var/account/pacct, and 'lastcomm' and 'sa'
answer which account ran what, and when: the question an investigation
asks first, and one auditd answers only for the system calls it was
told to watch.

This is a hardening opportunity rather than a weakness, so it stays
informational: no distribution installs it, and the record it keeps
costs disk space and a little CPU on a busy host. Where who-ran-what
matters (a shared machine, a jump host, a server under compliance),
install it and enable its service; it rotates its file through
logrotate on every distribution that packages it.
